hub.com/users/yamen-haddad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-16T19:53:52Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T01:10:30Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-18732](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-18732)\n### Description\n\nYSQL indices have a state in pg catalog indicating whether the index can be relied on to serve reads or not. When the index is first created, it is initially invalid, and the state is updated later. \nIn case of creating a backup, ysql_dump does not include invalid indices in the dump sql output. \nHowever, the created snapshot includes all the DocDB tables in the snapshot, including the indices and regardless of whether or not they are valid.\n\nThis leads to creating a backup that will fail at restore with the following error:\n\n`\n[m-1] W1016 18:15:52.951835 74817 catalog_manager_ext.cc:2189] Did not find a corresponding table at restore side for the table 000034d4000030008000000000004005 from backup.\n`\n\nThis is because the DocDB table with id `000034d4000030008000000000004005` corresponds to the invalid index that hasn't been included in the dump from the backup side.\nIt is worth mentioning that the restore only fails with the new backup workflow, where we support backups during DDLs.\nThe old workflow deals correctly with invalid indices.\nWe should fix the issue by skipping the DocDB tables that correspond to invalid indices at export_snapshot. \nThe check of whether the index is valid or not happens by reading the pg catalog as of the consistent `snapshot_ht`.\n\nThe issue was detected by the failing tests:\n\n```\nybd release --cxx-test tools_yb-backup-cross-feature-test --gtest_filter CrossColocationTests/YBBackupCrossColocation.TestYSQLRestoreWithInvalidIndex/0\n\nybd release --cxx-test tools_yb-backup-cross-feature-test --gtest_filter TableRewriteTests/YBBackupTestWithTableRewrite.TestYSQLBackupAndRestoreAfterFailedRewrite/0\n````\n\n### Issue Type\n\nkind/bug\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [x] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-18732]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-18732?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/28986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/28986/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}